{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117935","id":3460969737,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7OSjUJ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117935","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117935.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117935.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117935","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117935/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117935/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117935/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/12ffe86707418ece71cf0a2e9a9aa4d3f3629e28","number":117935,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add a power-of-2 hotkeys to the 3D scene grid.","user":{"login":"Yarwin","id":5611207,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEyMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611207?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin","html_url":"https://github.com/Yarwin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yarwin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nOne outlined in: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14555. Tl;dr – make grid follow snap + give shortcuts to multiply said grid by power of 2. It follows the very same logic as canvas item plugin – i.e. snap menu is in the same place, shortcuts are the same and whatnot.\r\n\r\nBased on previous @Calinou work: https://github.com/Calinou/godot/commit/4eecb50f12ffd7f1414b0f78adf3aa30b361477b#diff-57832e09092105245d5eaa89d7834a30f5c6bd6e5b5166450fde12f61a585d4cL6256. \r\n\r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary> Manual testing / how it looks in action </summary>\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5b83117c-5f2f-41c4-92ab-1ecd2d75b6a9\r\n\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n## Other things / followups etc\r\n\r\nAs outlined in the proposal – exposing a menu with the info about current snap would be nice, as well as standardizing shortcuts to ones used by the Trenchbroom (i.e. `+`\\\\`-` instead of `*`\\\\`/`). This PR is fairly conservative – we should create a proper design beforehand. Whatever we set on both modes should use the same language.\r\n\r\nWe should standardize rulers as well.  The 2D one packs in a lot of useful info, while 3D one is very basic.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"319\" height=\"246\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e35e02ef-fe86-4cee-8bcb-ea7d732f41e7\" />\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283